@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Browser extension privacy";
    var supportAddress = Configuration["Email:SupportAddress"] ?? "support@example.test";
}

<section class="workspace-hero privacy-hero">
    <div class="shell workspace-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Browser extension privacy</p>
            <h1>Your click defines<br />the boundary.</h1>
            <p>What the Job Application Tracker extension reads and where it sends information.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button-secondary" asp-action="BrowserExtension">Extension overview</a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="workspace-content privacy-workspace">
    <div class="shell privacy-layout">
        <article class="detail-card privacy-intro">
            <p class="mini-label">The short version</p>
            <h2>Extract and Fill start when you choose them.</h2>
            <p>Extract reads the active tab's job advertisement and opens a private review draft. Fill reads your connected tracker profile and writes matching information into blank fields on the employer's form.</p>
        </article>

        <div class="privacy-grid">
            <article class="detail-card">
                <p class="mini-label">Information handled</p>
                <h2>Website content and page address</h2>
                <p>A capture may include the page URL, role title, employer, location, employment type, salary, job reference, closing date, and visible job description.</p>
                <p>An optional application-portal URL can be entered manually on the review page. The extension does not extract or infer that URL.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="detail-card">
                <p class="mini-label">Purpose and consent</p>
                <h2>Saved applicant profile</h2>
                <p>You choose which contact details, work experience, education, certifications, links and answers to save. The tracker encrypts your saved profile. Connecting the extension grants temporary read access that you can revoke from your profile.</p>
                <p>Résumé import reads an uploaded file to suggest profile fields and discards the file after processing. Review the suggestions and choose Save profile to keep them.</p>
                <p>The employer's site can read values written into its form before you submit. Review the form and handle consent and submission yourself.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="detail-card">
                <p class="mini-label">Transfer and storage</p>
                <h2>HTTPS to the private tracker</h2>
                <p>The configured HTTPS tracker validates and encrypts the capture, returns a random single-use handoff token, and never places job content in the browser URL. The handoff expires after 10 minutes and is removed when redeemed or during cleanup; the resulting owner-scoped review draft expires after 24 hours if it is not confirmed.</p>
                <p>Confirmed applications follow the tracker retention choices described in the main privacy summary.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="detail-card">
                <p class="mini-label">What is not collected</p>
                <h2>No passive browsing history</h2>
                <p>The extension does not monitor background tabs, read cookies or passwords, collect analytics, run advertising trackers, or capture pages without an explicit click.</p>
                <p>It does not contact an AI service or sell captured information.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="detail-card">
                <p class="mini-label">Permissions</p>
                <h2>Active tab and tracker access</h2>
                <p><strong>activeTab</strong> provides temporary access to the tab where you invoke the extension. <strong>scripting</strong> runs the extraction or fill action. <strong>storage</strong> holds the capture and profile connection in browser-session memory. The extension requests access to the tracker origin for profile retrieval.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="detail-card">
                <p class="mini-label">Limited use</p>
                <h2>No unrelated use or sharing</h2>
                <p>Information handled by the extension is used to provide job extraction, review and application autofill.</p>
                <p>The extension's use of information complies with the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
            </article>
        </div>

        <article class="detail-card extension-contact-card">
            <p class="mini-label">Questions or deletion requests</p>
            <h2>Contact the tracker administrator</h2>
            <p>Email <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:@supportAddress">@supportAddress</a> for extension privacy questions, account-wide access, or deletion requests.</p>
        </article>

        <p class="privacy-updated">Effective and last updated 25 August 2026.</p>
    </div>
</section>
